comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T13:08:12.765Z",codex-agent,"Privacy preflight distinguishes environment variable references and short plain token-accounting prose from credential-shaped literals. Password and key assignments, token prefixes, JWTs, private keys, authenticated URLs and unapproved emails refuse before persistence. Synthetic frontmatter containing a fake credential is covered."
  "2026-10-19T14:01:04.911Z",codex-agent,Import preflight aggregates all offending relative filenames and line numbers with matched privacy classes before any writes; remedies identify editing and --allow-email. Native help now provides descriptions and realistic examples for every operand and option.
  "2026-10-19T14:32:09.525Z",codex-agent,"Final synthetic and packed acceptance: import reports every offending relative file and line with the matched email/credential class before any writes, and names editing plus --allow-email remedies. Native import help now renders real source/format descriptions and examples. The pinned SDK supports argument and flag descriptions; no help-description gap."
